n_full":"Comcast Corporation operates as a media and technology company worldwide. The company operates through Residential Connectivity & Platforms, Business Services Connectivity, Media, Studios, and Theme Parks segments. Its Residential Connectivity & Platforms segment provides residential broadband and wireless connectivity services, residential and business video services, sky-branded entertainment television networks, and advertising. The Business Services Connectivity segment offers connectivity services for small business locations, which include broadband, wireline voice, and wireless services; and ethernet network services for medium-sized customers and larger enterprises. Its Media segment operates NBCUniversal's national and regional cable networks; the NBC and Telemundo broadcast networks and owned local broadcast television stations; and Peacock, a direct-to-consumer streaming services. The company also operates international television networks comprising the Sky Sports networks, as well as other digital properties. Its Studios segment operates NBCUniversal and Sky film and television studio production and distribution operations. The Theme Parks segment operates Universal theme parks in Orlando, Florida; Hollywood, California; Osaka, Japan; and Beijing, China. It also offers a consolidated streaming platforms under the Philadelphia Flyers and the Xfinity Mobile Arena in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania; and Xumo. Comcast Corporation was founded in 1963 and is headquartered in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian L. Roberts | Chairman & Co-CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $11.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 179K people. Revenue per employee of $691K ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $122K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Comcast Corporation is a large-cap communication services business with a $89.3B market cap on $123.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $21.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.68\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 13.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 76% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 48% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","18 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"UPS or Comcast: I Can Only Pick One Dividend Stock for the Next 10 Years. Here\u2019s Mine","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ups-comcast-only-pick-one-144809253.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794581289.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"How to watch Loyola-Chicago vs. Colorado State men's basketball","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/watch-loyola-chicago-vs-colorado-233115000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794613339.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Obama CIA Director John Brennan's Son, 40, Arrested for Alleged Possession of Child Abuse Material","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/obama-cia-director-john-brennans-222013000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794610762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.91,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Former CIA Director John Brennan's son arrested after FBI uncovers dozens of alleged child porn images","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/former-cia-director-john-brennans-203632000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794610008.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.735,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Hollywood Theme Park Breaks the $1,000 Annual Pass Barrier","source":"aol.com","link":"htt