 52-week range, 23% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 33% and a beta of 0.65, it is more defensive than the market.","Liquidity is deep, with about $644.4M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 31% in the 2020 crash, 43% in the 2022 bear market and 50% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 76% below its DCF fair value of $107, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 35%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $74.84 to $155 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Communication Services peers: P/E 8.0 vs 15.4, EV/EBITDA 5.0 vs 9.9 and P/FCF 4.1 vs 11.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 25% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 24.5% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 12.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 22 covering analysts target $27.98 on average, 11% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 9% earns above the cost of capital of 7.0%, but the 2pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.25).","It converts 18% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.68x.","ROE of 21% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.0% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.4x net debt to EBITDA ($9.5B of cash against $98.9B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 4.7x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.33 in the distress zone.","The current ratio of 0.88 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.6% over 3 years, 3.6% over 5 years and 5.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 28% of profits supports about 2.4% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 7.1% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 13%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (9.5% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 20, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and institutions hold 93%.","It returns 13.5% a year to shareholders (8.0% in buybacks and 5.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 4.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 18 consecutive years, raising it 3.4% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 179,000 employees, each generates about $691K of revenue, in line with the Communication Services median, and revenue has grown 8.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $122K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $11.7M (17x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $7K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":71,"head":"Invest: trades 76% below fair value of $107; FCF margin 17.7%.","pros":["Composite 51, above the 39 line (gates 15/25)","Trades 76% below fair value of $107","FCF margin 17.7%","P/E 8.0x vs sector 15.4x","EV/EBITDA 5.0x vs sector 9.9x"],"cons":["Altman Z in the distress zone (1.33)"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":90.64,"vc":{"base":106.64,"base_src":"dcf","bear":74.84,"bull":154.87,"alt_median":54.96,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.3945,"dispersion":0.3491,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (35% dispersion)","DCF is 139% above the other models' median ($54.96)"]},"med":{"pe":15.4103,"ev_ebitda":9.933,"pfcf":11.114,"pb":1.9265,"roic":0.0625,"gross_margin":0.5464,"fcf_margin":0.1304,"div_yield":0.0323}},"mc_quantiles":[54.33,67.33,74.84,80.77,84.87,89.04,93.02,97.13,100.62,104.27,107.33,112.48,117.06,121.19,126.68,131.55,137.6,146.21,154.87,174.54,216.39],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.524,"discount_rate":0.373,"terminal_growth":0.057,"exit_multipl